# Security & Authentication — DonateNow

> Reference: [PRD.mdc](../PRD.mdc) | [architecture.mdc](./architecture.mdc) | [ERD.mdc](./ERD.mdc)

---

## 1. Authentication Strategy

### Public Pages (No Auth Required)
- Donation Page (`/`)
- Thank-You Page (`/thank-you`)

### Admin Panel (Auth Required)
- Admin Dashboard (`/admin`)
- Donor Log (`/admin/donors`)

### Auth Implementation
- Provider: **Supabase Auth**
- Method: Email + Password (Admin only)
- Session: JWT-based, stored in HTTP-only cookie
- Session Expiry: 24 hours
- Refresh Token: Enabled via Supabase

### Admin Access Control
- Role: `admin`
- Default Admin: Seeded during setup
- No public registration for admin
- Admin accounts created manually via Supabase dashboard or seed script

---

## 2. API Security

### Razorpay Integration
- API Keys stored in environment variables (`.env.local`)
- **Never expose `key_secret` to client-side**
- `key_id` is public-safe (used in frontend checkout)
- `key_secret` used only in server-side API routes

### Webhook Security
- Razorpay webhook signature verification is **mandatory**
- Use `razorpay.webhooks.verify()` with `webhook_secret`
- Reject all requests with invalid signatures
- Webhook endpoint: `/api/webhook/razorpay`
- Allowed IPs: Razorpay IP whitelist (production only)

### API Route Protection
```
Public Routes (No Auth):
  POST /api/create-order        → Create Razorpay order
  POST /api/verify-payment      → Verify payment signature
  POST /api/webhook/razorpay    → Razorpay webhook handler

Protected Routes (Admin Auth Required):
  GET  /api/admin/donations     → Fetch donor log
  GET  /api/admin/stats         → Fetch dashboard stats
```

### Rate Limiting
- `/api/create-order`: 10 requests/minute per IP
- `/api/webhook/razorpay`: No rate limit (Razorpay server)
- `/api/admin/*`: 60 requests/minute per session

