## 3. Data Protection

### Donor Data Classification
| Data Field | Sensitivity | Storage | Encryption |
|---|---|---|---|
| Donor Name | Medium | Supabase | At rest (Supabase default) |
| Donor Email | Medium | Supabase | At rest (Supabase default) |
| Donor Phone | Medium | Supabase | At rest (Supabase default) |
| Donation Amount | Low | Supabase | At rest (Supabase default) |
| Razorpay Payment ID | Medium | Supabase | At rest (Supabase default) |
| Razorpay Order ID | Low | Supabase | At rest (Supabase default) |
| Card/UPI Details | Critical | **Never stored** | Handled by Razorpay |

### Key Rules
1. **Never store card numbers, CVV, or UPI PINs** — Razorpay handles all payment data
2. Store only Razorpay reference IDs (payment_id, order_id, signature)
3. Supabase Row Level Security (RLS) enabled on all tables
4. Admin-only read access on `donations` table
5. No public read/write on any table

---

## 4. Supabase Row Level Security (RLS)

### `donations` Table
```sql
-- Enable RLS
ALTER TABLE donations ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- Allow insert from service role only (webhook/API route)
CREATE POLICY "Service role can insert donations"
  ON donations FOR INSERT
  TO service_role
  WITH CHECK (true);

-- Allow read for authenticated admin users only
CREATE POLICY "Admin can read donations"
  ON donations FOR SELECT
  TO authenticated
  USING (auth.jwt() ->> 'role' = 'admin');

-- No public access
-- No update or delete allowed
```

### `causes` Table
```sql
-- Public can read causes (for donation page)
CREATE POLICY "Public can read causes"
  ON causes FOR SELECT
  TO anon
  USING (is_active = true);

-- Only admin can modify causes
CREATE POLICY "Admin can manage causes"
  ON causes FOR ALL
  TO authenticated
  USING (auth.jwt() ->> 'role' = 'admin');
```

