## 5. Environment Variables Security

### Storage Rules
1. All secrets in `.env.local` (never committed to git)
2. `.env.local` added to `.gitignore`
3. Production secrets in Vercel Environment Variables (encrypted)
4. Separate keys for test mode and production mode

### Required Secrets
```
NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID     → Public (safe for client)
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET             → Server-only (never expose)
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET         → Server-only (webhook verification)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL        → Public (safe for client)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY   → Public (safe with RLS)
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY       → Server-only (bypasses RLS)
```

### Naming Convention
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` → Safe for client-side exposure
- No prefix → Server-side only, never bundled to client

